<chapter xml:id="ch-when-research-travels" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>When Research Travels: Seedballs, Scale and the Next Questions</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      The closing <q>Putting It All Together</q> chapter follows a promising option from controlled testing into diverse farms and wider use. The sequence brings earlier judgements together where they become consequential: comparisons, scale, measurement, variation and farmer responsibility. Wider use creates further questions about management, labour, costs and the whole farm.
    </p>
  </introduction>

  <section xml:id="sec-when-research-travels-source-notes">
    <title>Source notes</title>
    <p>
      <alert>Related transcripts:</alert> Reflections on Next Steps; RMS and Multilevel Data; On-farm Agricultural Trials; Measurements; CRFS Proxy Variables.
    </p>
    <p>
      <alert>Source position:</alert> No complete seedball transcript is recorded in the current source map. Publications and programme records provide the documented sequence; missing accounts of decisions must remain explicit. Focused accounts from Ali Maman Aminou, Hannatou Moussa Oumarou and other participants could strengthen those transitions.
    </p>
  </section>
</chapter>
